    "hero_jr47q9": {
      "type": "hero",
      "blocks": {
        "slide_4nXUWA": {
          "type": "slide",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Screenshot_2026-02-20_at_2.59.47_pm.png",
            "subheading": "",
            "title": "Six Years, Six Artists: GSM Artists Collective Returns to the Affordable Art Fair Melbourne 2026",
            "text": "<p><em>Celebrating our 6th year running with a lineup that blends returning favourites and exciting new talent</em></p><p>Gotham Studios Melbourne (GSM) Artists Collective is returning to the Affordable Art Fair, marking our 6th year with the fair and a homecoming to the city where it all began. This August, we’re bringing a refreshed stand, new perspectives, and a growing community of artists, anchored by a lineup that brings together returning favourites and a new wave of talent joining the Collective for the first time.</p><p>Returning artists Lisa Saad, Sebnem Gencer, Sheng Yi Lee, Luca Chiaravalle, and Francesca Laude are joined this year by Amanda Forsyth, broadening the range of work, perspective, and practice on show.</p><p><em>“Every year our stand evolves, and I’m incredibly proud of what we’ve built together. Welcoming fresh voices alongside familiar ones is what keeps the Collective alive. It’s the best of both worlds for collectors and for us,” said Lisa Saad, lead of the Gotham Studios Melbourne Artists Collective.</em></p><p>Gotham Studios Melbourne has spent decades delivering standout visuals for global brands, but our Artists Collective is where we celebrate artistic exploration beyond the studio. It’s where personal expression takes centre stage, and where emerging and established artists share the same platform. Something this year’s blend of returning and new artists captures perfectly.</p><p>We can’t wait to connect, share our latest work, and bring art that sparks conversation long after the fair ends. Find us at Stand H1.</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_position_large": "center start",
            "text_position_mobile": "start",
